            <ArticleTitle>Dissection of the aortic root presenting as a double aortic valve.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>275-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of aortic root dissection in a middle-aged male without history of recent trauma, presenting as a critical aortic regurgitation due to right cusp dislodgement. The intraoperative transesophageal echocardiogram revealed the &quot;double aortic valve&quot; sign suggestive of low dissection, which proved to extend to both coronary arteries.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
